{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788391293627,"sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b6f57e46bcf4afd7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/tsconfig.test.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/tsconfig.test.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n3:   \"compilerOptions\": {\n4:     \"rootDir\": \".\",\n5:     \"noEmit\": true,\n6:     \"types\": [\"node\", \"vitest/globals\"]\n7:   },\n8:   \"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"tests/**/*\"]\n9: }\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"types\": [\"node\", \"vitest/globals\"]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"tests/**/*\"]\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/tsconfig.test.json","text":"{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"types\": [\"node\", \"vitest/globals\"]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"tests/**/*\"]\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"tsconfig.test.json","time":{"start":1788391293527,"end":1788391293621}},"id":"prt_0646d82040016OqvOCsVrAov6M","sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","messageID":"msg_0646d7f5d001EQBEX9OoKESkx9"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788391293654,"sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bc14cb3711dedeee","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/vitest.config.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/vitest.config.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n2: \n3: export default defineConfig({\n4:   test: {\n5:     globals: false,\n6:     environment: \"node\",\n7:     include: [\"tests/**/*.test.ts\"],\n8:   },\n9: });\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  test: {\n    globals: false,\n    environment: \"node\",\n    include: [\"tests/**/*.test.ts\"],\n  },\n});","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/vitest.config.ts","text":"import { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  test: {\n    globals: false,\n    environment: \"node\",\n    include: [\"tests/**/*.test.ts\"],\n  },\n});","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"vitest.config.ts","time":{"start":1788391293580,"end":1788391293642}},"id":"prt_0646d8267001Mr4Yz2zgL4JZtn","sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","messageID":"msg_0646d7f5d001EQBEX9OoKESkx9"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788391293698,"sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e91e3aa2c14783","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Book Collection API\n2: \n3: A REST API service for managing a book collection, written in TypeScript with\n4: Express and backed by SQLite (`better-sqlite3`).\n5: \n6: ## Features\n7: \n8: - `POST /books` — Create a new book\n9: - `GET /books` — List all books (supports `?author=` filtering, case-insensitive partial match)\n10: - `GET /books/{id}` — Get a single book by ID\n11: - `PUT /books/{id}` — Update a book (full replacement)\n12: - `DELETE /books/{id}` — Delete a book\n13: - `GET /health` — Health check endpoint\n14: \n15: ### Book fields\n16: \n17: | field   | type   | required | notes                                   |\n18: |---------|--------|----------|-----------------------------------------|\n19: | title   | string | yes      | non-empty                               |\n20: | author  | string | yes      | non-empty                               |\n21: | year    | number | no       | integer between 0 and (current year + 1) |\n22: | isbn    | string | no       |                                         |\n23: \n24: Responses are JSON. Appropriate HTTP status codes are used (`201` on create,\n25: `204` on delete, `400` on validation error, `404` when not found).\n26: \n27: ## Prerequisites\n28: \n29: - Node.js 18+ (developed on Node 22)\n30: - npm\n31: \n32: ## Setup\n33: \n34: ```bash\n35: npm install\n36: ```\n37: \n38: ## Build\n39: \n40: ```bash\n41: npm run build        # outputs compiled JS to ./dist\n42: ```\n43: \n44: ## Run\n45: \n46: Start the server (listens on port 3000 by default, uses `books.db` in the\n47: working directory):\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: npm start            # runs compiled output from dist/\n51: # or, for development with auto-reload:\n52: npm run dev\n53: ```\n54: \n55: Configuration via environment variables:\n56: \n57: | Variable  | default    | description                          |\n58: |-----------|------------|--------------------------------------|\n59: | `PORT`    | `3000`     | port the HTTP server listens on       |\n60: | `DB_PATH` | `books.db` | path to the SQLite database file      |\n61: \n62: Use `DB_PATH=:memory:` to run against an in-memory database.\n63: \n64: ## Test\n65: \n66: ```bash\n67: npm test             # runs the vitest suite once\n68: npm run test:watch   # runs in watch mode\n69: npm run typecheck     # type-checks source + tests without emitting\n70: ```\n71: \n72: The suite includes unit tests for input validation and integration tests that\n73: exercise the full Express app over HTTP via `supertest` using an in-memory\n74: SQLite database.\n75: \n76: ## Example requests\n77: \n78: Create a book:\n79: \n80: ```bash\n81: curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \\\n82:   -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n83:   -d '{\"title\":\"1984\",\"author\":\"George Orwell\",\"year\":1949,\"isbn\":\"978-0451524935\"}'\n84: ```\n85: \n86: List books, optionally filtered by author:\n87: \n88: ```bash\n89: curl -sS http://localhost:3000/books\n90: curl -sS 'http://localhost:3000/books?author=orwell'\n91: ```\n92: \n93: ## Project layout\n94: \n95: ```\n96: src/\n97:   db.ts          # SQLite data layer (BookStore)\n98:   validation.ts # input validation for book payloads\n99:   app.ts         # Express application (route definitions)\n100:   index.ts       # server entry point\n101: tests/\n102:   health.test.ts     # health endpoint test\n103:   books.test.ts      # API integration tests\n104:   validation.test.ts # validation unit tests\n105: ```\n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Book Collection API\n\nA REST API service for managing a book collection, written in TypeScript with\nExpress and backed by SQLite (`better-sqlite3`).\n\n## Features\n\n- `POST /books` — Create a new book\n- `GET /books` — List all books (supports `?author=` filtering, case-insensitive partial match)\n- `GET /books/{id}` — Get a single book by ID\n- `PUT /books/{id}` — Update a book (full replacement)\n- `DELETE /books/{id}` — Delete a book\n- `GET /health` — Health check endpoint\n\n### Book fields\n\n| field   | type   | required | notes                                   |\n|---------|--------|----------|-----------------------------------------|\n| title   | string | yes      | non-empty                               |\n| author  | string | yes      | non-empty                               |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# Book Collection API\n\nA REST API service for managing a book collection, written in TypeScript with\nExpress and backed by SQLite (`better-sqlite3`).\n\n## Features\n\n- `POST /books` — Create a new book\n- `GET /books` — List all books (supports `?author=` filtering, case-insensitive partial match)\n- `GET /books/{id}` — Get a single book by ID\n- `PUT /books/{id}` — Update a book (full replacement)\n- `DELETE /books/{id}` — Delete a book\n- `GET /health` — Health check endpoint\n\n### Book fields\n\n| field   | type   | required | notes                                   |\n|---------|--------|----------|-----------------------------------------|\n| title   | string | yes      | non-empty                               |\n| author  | string | yes      | non-empty                               |\n| year    | number | no       | integer between 0 and (current year + 1) |\n| isbn    | string | no       |                                         |\n\nResponses are JSON. Appropriate HTTP status codes are used (`201` on create,\n`204` on delete, `400` on validation error, `404` when not found).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Node.js 18+ (developed on Node 22)\n- npm\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n## Build\n\n```bash\nnpm run build        # outputs compiled JS to ./dist\n```\n\n## Run\n\nStart the server (listens on port 3000 by default, uses `books.db` in the\nworking directory):\n\n```bash\nnpm start            # runs compiled output from dist/\n# or, for development with auto-reload:\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nConfiguration via environment variables:\n\n| Variable  | default    | description                          |\n|-----------|------------|--------------------------------------|\n| `PORT`    | `3000`     | port the HTTP server listens on       |\n| `DB_PATH` | `books.db` | path to the SQLite database file      |\n\nUse `DB_PATH=:memory:` to run against an in-memory database.\n\n## Test\n\n```bash\nnpm test             # runs the vitest suite once\nnpm run test:watch   # runs in watch mode\nnpm run typecheck     # type-checks source + tests without emitting\n```\n\nThe suite includes unit tests for input validation and integration tests that\nexercise the full Express app over HTTP via `supertest` using an in-memory\nSQLite database.\n\n## Example requests\n\nCreate a book:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"1984\",\"author\":\"George Orwell\",\"year\":1949,\"isbn\":\"978-0451524935\"}'\n```\n\nList books, optionally filtered by author:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS http://localhost:3000/books\ncurl -sS 'http://localhost:3000/books?author=orwell'\n```\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\nsrc/\n  db.ts          # SQLite data layer (BookStore)\n  validation.ts # input validation for book payloads\n  app.ts         # Express application (route definitions)\n  index.ts       # server entry point\ntests/\n  health.test.ts     # health endpoint test\n  books.test.ts      # API integration tests\n  validation.test.ts # validation unit tests\n```","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":105,"totalLines":105,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1788391293649,"end":1788391293690}},"id":"prt_0646d82a8001JPgP7JmHNTpJAL","sessionID":"ses_f9b92ae3fffeRZej9FS7ZTNZkO","messageID":"msg_0646d7f5d001EQBEX9OoKESkx9"}}
